course: dictionary
lesson: 12296
title: Cooked: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cooked can work as a describing word or as an action word. As a describing word, cooked tells you food has been made ready to eat by heating it. «The cooked chicken smelled delicious.» Here cooked describes the chicken.
explain: Cooked can also be the past form of the verb cook. Cook, cooks, cooking and cooked all come from the same idea. «She cooked dinner for the whole family.» Cooked tells you the cooking happened in the past.
explain: To find which job cooked is doing, look at the words around it. If it describes food, such as «the cooked rice», it is a describing word. If someone did the cooking, such as «Dad cooked», it is the past form of the verb. Swap in «made ready to eat by heating» to check.
fact: Cooked means made ready to eat by heating, like boiled, baked or fried food.
fact: Cooked is also the past form of cook: «She cooked dinner».
fact: Phrases you may see: cooked through, home-cooked, well cooked, undercooked, overcooked.
fact: Chicken must be cooked all the way through to kill germs, and raw chicken must not touch cooked food.
fact: Cooking changes food in a way that cannot be undone: a cooked egg cannot become raw again.
exercise: «The cooked chicken smelled delicious.» What does cooked mean here? | Washed and dried | Still raw and cold from the fridge | Thrown away | *Made ready to eat by heating
exercise: «Dad cooked pancakes on Sunday morning.» What kind of word is cooked here? | A describing word | A word for a colour | *An action word in the past | A name for a place
exercise: «Make sure the chicken is cooked through before you eat it.» What does cooked through mean? | Left out to cool | *Heated all the way through | Cut into small pieces | Covered in sauce
test: «We ate a home-cooked meal together.» What does home-cooked suggest? | Bought ready-made from a shop | Eaten outside in a park | Burnt and thrown away | *Made at home by someone in the family
test: «A cooked egg can never become raw again.» Why not? | The fridge stops it from changing | Eggs are never raw | Eggs only change when they are cold | *Cooking changes food in a way that cannot be undone
exam: «Mum cooked the rice, and now it is ready to eat.» What does cooked show here? | It shows the rice is a different colour | It shows the rice is cold | *It shows a past action: the rice was made ready to eat by heating | It shows the rice is raw
